{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_013","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Dynamic Non-Fungible Tokens (dNFTs)","location_hint":"paragraph 58","char_start":1437,"char_end":1472,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_014","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Copy page as Markdown for LLMs","location_hint":"paragraph 82","char_start":1977,"char_end":2007,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_015","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"The XRP Ledger natively supports non-fungible tokens (NFTs, or “nifties” in the vernacular). Non-fungible tokens serve to encode ownership of unique physical, non-physical, or purely digital goods, such as works of art or in-game items.","location_hint":"paragraph 93","char_start":2265,"char_end":2501,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_016","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Requires the NonFungibleTokensV1_1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 94","char_start":2503,"char_end":2560,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_017","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"To represent digital assets similar to these, use the XRP Ledger&#x27;s Non-Fungible Tokens feature (sometimes referred to by its standards draft number, XLS-20 ).","location_hint":"paragraph 95","char_start":2562,"char_end":2725,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_018","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"On the XRP Ledger, an NFT is represented as a NFToken object. An NFT is a unique, indivisible unit that is not used for payments. Users can mint (create), hold, buy, sell, and burn (destroy) NFTs.","location_hint":"paragraph 97","char_start":2751,"char_end":2947,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_019","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"The ledger stores up to 32 NFTs owned by the same account in a single NFTokenPage object to save space. As a result, the owner&#x27;s reserve requirement for NFTs only increases when the ledger needs to make a new page to store additional tokens.","location_hint":"paragraph 98","char_start":2949,"char_end":3195,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_020","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Accounts can also name a Broker or an Authorized Minter who can sell or mint NFTs on their behalf.","location_hint":"paragraph 99","char_start":3197,"char_end":3295,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_021","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"NFTs have several immutable settings that are defined when the token is minted. These include:","location_hint":"paragraph 100","char_start":3297,"char_end":3391,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_022","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Identifying data that uniquely defines the token.","location_hint":"paragraph 101","char_start":3395,"char_end":3444,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_023","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Whether the issuer can burn the token, regardless of who currently holds it.","location_hint":"paragraph 102","char_start":3446,"char_end":3522,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_024","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Whether the holder of the token can transfer it to others. (An NFT can always be sent to or from the issuer directly.)","location_hint":"paragraph 103","char_start":3524,"char_end":3642,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_025","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"If transfers are allowed, the issuer can charge a transfer fee as a percentage of the sale price. If there is a transfer fee, the NFT can only be traded for tokens for which the issuer has a trust line.","location_hint":"paragraph 104","char_start":3644,"char_end":3846,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_026","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Whether the holder can sell the NFT for fungible token amounts, or only for XRP.","location_hint":"paragraph 105","char_start":3848,"char_end":3928,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_027","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"Anyone can create a new NFT using the NFTokenMint transaction . The NFT lives on the NFTokenPage object of the issuing account. Either the owner or an interested party can send a NFTokenCreateOffer transaction to propose buying or selling the NFT; the ledger tracks the proposed transfer as a NFTokenOffer object , and deletes the NFTokenOffer when either side accepts or cancels the offer. If the NFT is transferable, it can be traded multiple times between accounts.","location_hint":"paragraph 107","char_start":3947,"char_end":4415,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_028","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"You can destroy an NFT you own using the NFTokenBurn transaction . If the issuer minted the token with the tfBurnable flag enabled, the issuer can also burn the token, regardless of the current owner. (This could be useful, for example, for a token that represents a ticket to an event that is used up at some point.)","location_hint":"paragraph 108","char_start":4417,"char_end":4734,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_029","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"For more info about transferring NFTs, see Trading NFTs on the XRP Ledger .","location_hint":"paragraph 109","char_start":4738,"char_end":4813,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ec3eb93321a7_030","source_id":"src_ec3eb93321a7","source_hash":"b1681d7af5d9e2f44bbd01e924082fea12feb7688a8f0578fafb5a774ab1f62a","text":"NFTs on the XRP Ledger NFT Lifecycle","location_hint":"paragraph 117","char_start":4968,"char_end":5004,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T10:19:50.900Z"}
